surement: a typed identity through one generic no-argument big operator, checked on the empty integer and float sums with their run-time types, a generic dot-shaped reduction and the empty products. Its walk half is the flattening rung's test (the judgement's § 7 check 1, on all eight leaves); its candidate spelling, the library's checked `cast[\T\]`, is the one this judgement measured failing on the compiled path (row 426), so the compiled half waits on row 426 or a checker refinement of the witness branch (§ 7 check 3), before the switch-over; and its brief's unchanged-call-site requirement is superseded by Pavol's approval of the two C4 diffs (POSITIONS 2026-09-26, answer 7, the catch-all). Row 426 closed with row 351 in climb batch 6.5 rung G. The witness through the repaired `cast` answers each static argument's identity compiled (`compiler_tests/WitnessIdentityRungG`), and the one library's `ZZ32` and `RR64` branches pass a typed binding, `v: ZZ32 = 0` then `cast[\T\](v)`, whose value under walk is unchanged (`compile-ladder/rung-generic-runtime/probes/identity-walk-before.txt`, `identity-walk-after.txt`). The checker refinement was not needed. A compiled `SUM` end to end waits for the switch-over.

